CAT = "sgm5Faa"; SEG = "FAA"
Q = [
('Which law is the main statute governing financial advisers in Singapore?',
 'The Financial Advisers Act', ['The Securities and Futures Act', 'The Insurance Act 1966', 'The Companies Act 1967'],
 'The Financial Advisers Act 2001 (FAA) and its Financial Advisers Regulations govern financial advisory services. The Securities and Futures Act covers capital markets dealing, exchanges and market conduct.'),
('Which body administers the Financial Advisers Act?',
 'The Monetary Authority of Singapore', ['The Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority', 'The Singapore Exchange', 'The Central Provident Fund Board'],
 'MAS licenses and supervises financial advisers, issues the notices and guidelines made under the FAA, and can take enforcement action. SGX is a market operator, not the FAA regulator.'),
('A person who carries on business as a financial adviser in Singapore must, unless exempt:',
 "Hold a financial adviser's licence", ['Register with the Singapore Exchange', 'Hold a capital markets services licence', 'Join a trade association first'],
 'The FAA requires a licence from MAS to act as a financial adviser. Some institutions already supervised by MAS are exempt from holding the licence but must still follow the conduct rules.'),
('Which of these is an exempt financial adviser rather than a licensed one?',
 'A licensed bank', ['A firm set up only to sell funds', 'An independent advisory company', 'A sole adviser trading on his own'],
 "MAS's FAQs on the FAA list banks, merchant banks, finance companies, insurance companies, registered insurance brokers and capital markets services licence holders as exempt from holding a financial adviser's licence, though they must still follow the FAA's business conduct requirements."),
('A person who provides financial advisory services on behalf of a financial adviser is called its:',
 'Representative', ['Principal officer', 'Trustee', 'Introducing broker'],
 "Under the FAA, an individual who provides financial advisory services for a licensed or exempt financial adviser is its representative, and the financial adviser is the representative's principal."),
('Before an individual may act as an appointed representative, the principal must ensure that the individual is:',
 'Fit and proper for the role', ['A shareholder of the principal', 'A Singapore citizen', 'Employed full time for a year'],
 "The principal is responsible for checking that its representative is fit and proper and meets MAS's competency requirements before lodging the appointment."),
('Where can a member of the public check whether a person is an appointed representative?',
 "MAS's register of representatives", ['The Registry of Companies', 'The Singapore Government Gazette', "The CPF Board's member portal"],
 "Under the Representative Notification Framework, the principal notifies MAS before appointing a representative, and the representative's name and the services he may provide are entered in MAS's public register of representatives, so clients can check who they are dealing with."),
("Under MAS's competency notice, a representative must be at least how old?",
 '21', ['18', '19', '25'],
 'MAS Notice FAA-N26 sets the minimum entry requirements: at least 21 years old and a minimum academic qualification, unless an exemption applies.'),
("Which academic qualification meets MAS's minimum entry requirement for representatives?",
 'A polytechnic diploma', ["Four GCE 'O' Level passes", 'A Nitec certificate in business', 'A PSLE certificate'],
 "FAA-N26 accepts a GCE 'A' Level certificate with three H2 and two H1 passes, an International Baccalaureate Diploma, a Singapore polytechnic diploma, or an equivalent qualification."),
('Under the fit and proper guidelines, a representative who lacks the qualifications and experience for his role falls short on:',
 'Competence and capability', ['Financial soundness', 'Honesty and integrity', 'Reputation in the trade'],
 "MAS's Guidelines on Fit and Proper Criteria (FSG-G01) set three criteria: honesty, integrity and reputation; competence and capability; and financial soundness. A representative's educational qualifications, experience and relevant skills fall under competence and capability."),
("Which event is most likely to raise doubts about a representative's financial soundness?",
 'Being declared bankrupt', ['Taking a housing loan', 'Changing principal', 'Moving to part-time work'],
 'Under FSG-G01, being the subject of a bankruptcy petition, an undischarged bankruptcy or an unsatisfied judgment debt are factors in assessing financial soundness. Ordinary borrowing is not.'),
('A representative is convicted of an offence involving fraud. Under the fit and proper criteria this mainly affects his:',
 'Honesty and integrity', ['Financial soundness', 'Competence and capability', 'Product knowledge'],
 'Under FSG-G01, a conviction for any offence, and civil judgments or accepted liability for fraud, misrepresentation or dishonesty, are factors in assessing honesty, integrity and reputation.'),
('Who must assess on an ongoing basis whether its representatives remain fit and proper?',
 'The principal', ['The Life Insurance Association', 'The client', 'The product issuer'],
 'The principal must monitor its representatives and, under FAA-N26, include their continuing professional development in its assessment of whether they remain fit and proper.'),
('By the end of each calendar year after the first year of appointment, how many core CPD hours must a representative complete?',
 '6', ['4', '8', '10'],
 'FAA-N26 sets 6 core CPD hours a year: an IBF- or SCI-accredited course in ethics or rules and regulations, or a course run by the CPF Board on CPF matters.'),
('A representative advises on a range of investment products, not only mortgage reducing term or group term policies. How many supplementary CPD hours apply each year?',
 '24', ['10', '16', '30'],
 'FAA-N26 requires 24 supplementary CPD hours for advising on investment products generally, and 10 for representatives who deal only in mortgage reducing term assurance or group term life policies.'),
("Which activity does NOT count towards a representative's CPD hours?",
 'Researching products for clients', ['An accredited ethics course', 'A product seminar before launch', 'A documented e-learning course'],
 'CPD covers lectures, conferences, workshops, courses, pre-launch product seminars and e-learning with clear outcomes, but not work that is part of the job, such as researching products for clients.'),
('A representative falls ill and cannot finish CPD hours by year end. To avoid a breach she should:',
 'Tell her principal at once', ['Stop advising until January', 'Claim the hours anyway', 'Ask clients to vouch for her'],
 'Under FAA-N26, a representative who cannot meet the hours for reasons beyond her control must inform her principal immediately and complete the shortfall within 12 months.'),
('Who must keep the evidence that CPD hours were completed?',
 'The representative', ['The Monetary Authority of Singapore', 'The client', 'The course provider only'],
 'FAA-N26 requires each appointed representative to obtain and retain supporting evidence of the CPD training completed in the period.'),
("A financial adviser's licence is granted subject to conditions. Who may impose and vary those conditions?",
 'MAS', ['The Singapore Exchange', "The licensee's own board", 'The Ministry of Finance'],
 'MAS grants the licence and imposes conditions on it; many duties to notify MAS, such as of a material adverse change in financial position, are licence conditions. Adding a new type of regulated activity needs MAS approval of a variation under section 12 of the FAA.'),
('A representative wants to provide advice on behalf of a new principal. What must happen first?',
 'The new principal notifies MAS', ['He tells his clients by letter', 'His old licence is transferred', 'He re-registers with SGX'],
 "MAS's FAQs say the new principal must notify MAS of its intent to appoint the representative, and can do so only after the cessation of his appointment with the previous principal has taken effect."),
('Which activity is a type of financial advisory service under the FAA?',
 'Arranging life policies', ['Lending money to buy shares', 'Valuing a house for a bank', 'Auditing company accounts'],
 'The FAA covers advising on investment products, issuing analyses or reports on them, and arranging contracts of insurance for life policies, among others.'),
('MAS generally regards a person as carrying on a business of giving financial advice when the advice is given:',
 'Systematically, regularly and continuously', ['Only when a fee is charged', 'Only to five or more clients', 'Only in writing'],
 "MAS's FAQs say an activity done with system, repetition and continuity is carrying on a business, whether or not the person is paid for the advice. One-off advice is less likely to amount to carrying on a business."),
("The FAA's conduct requirements apply to an exempt financial adviser such as an insurer:",
 'Much as for licensed advisers', ['Not at all', 'Only for foreign clients', 'Only when MAS asks it to'],
 'Exempt financial advisers are exempt from holding a licence, not from the conduct rules: section 20(2) of the FAA applies sections 34 to 38 and others to them, and MAS notices such as FAA-N16 apply to both.'),
('A representative must provide financial advisory services only:',
 'For his own principal', ['For any adviser that pays him', 'For clients he refers himself', 'As a sole proprietor'],
 "MAS's one-representative-one-financial-adviser policy bars a representative on the public register from acting for more than one principal at a time (unless the principals are related corporations), so clients know where responsibility for complaints and redress rests."),
]
